    "done_when": "packages/imas-alambic/install/imasdb.sh IMASDB is the one install command, reading the layout names maps/current and ids from imas-alambic config rather than spelling them, and running every remote command under nice -n 19. Wheels for imas-alambic and nova-cocos are built here with uv build and copied over ssh jt-60sa. The private bundle ghcr.io/simon-mcintosh/imas-alambic-jt60sa:2026.10.07 is pulled here with oras and the gh token, copied to IMASDB/maps/2026.10.07, and IMASDB/maps/current points at it; no GitHub credential is placed on the server. On intr26-2: /home/SharedFolder/d240044 has mode 1755, every directory under IMASDB grants others r-x, every file grants others r--, and find IMASDB -perm -o+w prints nothing. The tool environment under IMASDB/tools holds imas-alambic as a wheel install, not editable, on a uv-managed CPython 3.12. IMASDB/bin/imas-alambic --version exits 0 both with PYTHONPATH set to the python/3.12 module site-packages and with it unset, and uv pip check against the tool environment reports no missing dependency. With no IMAS_ALAMBIC_* variable set, IMASDB/bin/imas-alambic config reports maps as IMASDB/maps/current and the IDS root as IMASDB/ids, both from IMAS_ALAMBIC_HOME, and the machine as jt-60sa inferred from the single reachable bundle. Outbound TLS on the server uses /etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt (GIT_SSL_CAINFO, SSL_CERT_FILE or uv native TLS), because the default CA path fails there. Only after every check above passes, the old ~/imas-alambic install is removed: its top-level entries are listed first, the removal prints what it removed, and ls afterwards shows it gone; nothing else in the account home is touched. Every remote command and its output is captured once to logs under the run directory.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "install imas-alambic from wheels into the shared IMASDB folder /home/SharedFolder/d240044/IMASDB on intr26-2 with packages/imas-alambic/install/imasdb.sh",
